    2. Draw the 30x30 frame (corner pixels, solid side rows/cols).
    3. Place 3-4 rectangular blobs of obj color in the interior, ensuring >=2 cell gaps and >=1 cell from frame.
    4. For each blob, choose 1-3 edges to receive a notch (at most 1 per edge). Pick a position >=2 from edge corners. Assign a direction matching that edge (top edge -> top, etc.).
    5. Carve each V-notch into the blob edge: remove the depth-2 staircase pattern [...,0,1,2,1,0,...] from the obj, creating 5 bg cells in a plus shape.
    6. Verify each notch's open arm faces bg (not another object) and the closed arm has obj support. The result is the input grid.
    7. To produce the output, fill each 5-cell plus with the color of its facing frame side.
